{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Not elohim.</b> Meaning: even they do not sacrifice to them on account of their being elohah, but rather to procure for themselves their needs and desires. And corresponding to what they do for idol worship, it says ״אֱלֹהִים לֹא יְדָעוּם״ — meaning, even though they do not know them, what the nature of the idols is, they worship them. And its saying ״חֲדָשִׁים מִקָּרֹב בָּאוּ״ etc. — see what I explained in the verse (Deuteronomy 13:7) ״כִּי יְסִיתְךָ אָחִיךָ״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:22.385043608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}